    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 all 38 tests pass, including the two new `Cp27Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `contactPreference` field on the owner response: `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nThe GET/POST owner responses are built from `OwnerDto`, which is generated from the OpenAPI spec and populated by MapStruct (`OwnerMapper`), matching how sibling derived fields like `membershipLevel` and `locality` work. Three changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` property (string enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generator emits `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum` and its getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/ContactPreference.java`** (new) \u2014 a small pure helper `of(Owner)` returning `\"EMAIL\"` when `owner.getEmail()` is non-null/non-empty, else `\"PHONE\"` \u2014 mirroring the existing `MembershipLevel`/`Locality` util pattern.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression that converts the util's string into the generated enum via `ContactPreferenceEnum.fromValue(...)`.\n\nNo new endpoint or function class was needed since this is a derived response field on the existing owner-read path.",
